  "method": "shadow-reaction LP with every exchange closed: max rate at which internal reactions alone reproduce the target reaction's net conversion",
  "caveats": [
    "Exchanges are closed so the claim is medium-independent; a bypass that needs an exchange is deliberately not counted. Conservative -- routes are missed, never invented.",
    "Full replaceability is required at the reaction's FULL capacity bound, which for a 1000-bound reaction is far more than any medium would ever demand. Conservative again.",
    "Only the loop-audited subset is trustworthy: with exchanges shut, futile cycles can fake a route. Unaudited counts are reported separately and should not be quoted.",
    "Replaceability of each disabled reaction is tested with the others also removed, so a gene's reactions cannot rescue each other."
  ],
